1. Purpose

The Product Backlog converts the approved requirements of the Competitive Programming Tracker into a prioritized list of product work.

Each backlog item represents a feature, capability, technical task, or improvement that can be planned and implemented during development.

The backlog will evolve throughout the project as requirements are refined and new information becomes available.

---

2. Backlog Priorities

We will use four priority levels:

| Priority      | Meaning                                        |
| ------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| P0 — Critical | Required for the basic application to function |
| P1 — High     | Required for the MVP                           |
| P2 — Medium   | Important but can be implemented after the MVP |
| P3 — Low      | Optional enhancement                           |

