18. Definition of Done

A backlog item will be considered **Done** when:

* The functionality has been implemented.
* The code follows the project's coding standards.
* Relevant tests have been created or updated.
* The feature has been tested successfully.
* No known critical defects remain.
* The change has been reviewed.
* The code has been committed to Git.
* The relevant GitHub Issue has been updated.
* Documentation has been updated where necessary.

---

19. Backlog Management

The backlog will be maintained throughout development.

Backlog items may be:

* Added
* Removed
* Reprioritized
* Split into smaller tasks
* Combined
* Modified based on new requirements

Changes to the backlog should be documented when they materially affect project scope.

